menu "Baby Health Monitor"

    config BABY_HEALTH_WIFI_SSID
        string "Wi-Fi SSID (2.4 GHz)"
        default ""
        help
            Configure the local Wi-Fi network. An empty SSID disables Wi-Fi
            and the HTTP metrics server, while sensor and display processing
            continue. The value is saved in the local, Git-ignored sdkconfig.

    config BABY_HEALTH_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Wi-Fi password"
        default ""
        help
            Password for the configured network. Leave empty for an open
            network. This is stored as plaintext in the local sdkconfig and
            compiled into the firmware; it is not encrypted secret storage.
            Never copy the real value into sdkconfig.defaults or commit it.

    config BABY_HEALTH_DISPLAY_ENABLED
        bool "Enable SSD1306 display (auto-detect on startup)"
        default y
        help
            Probe the configured OLED I2C address once at startup. If no
            device responds or initialization fails, continue without display
            output. A display update failure also disables further rendering.
            Reconnect the screen and restart the board to detect it again.

            Disable this option to skip all display I2C initialization and
            probing. Sensor sampling, Wi-Fi and Prometheus metrics are not
            affected by this option.

endmenu
